# Phoenix dev env vars
# ─────────────────────
#
# Copy to `.env` (project root, gitignored) and fill in the secrets.
# Vite auto-loads `.env` from the project root by default.
#
# `VITE_*` variables are exposed to the browser bundle by Vite (any var
# without that prefix is invisible to client code). Treat every value
# in `.env` like a shared secret — anything in here is one `cat` away
# from being leaked, so:
#   - rotate if leaked
#   - never check `.env` into source
#   - don't reuse production keys for local dev
#   - don't set the dev-only `VITE_APP_USER_NSEC` in any production build
#
# Required vs. optional is marked per-var. Bare-minimum to run the app:
# `VITE_BREEZ_API_KEY`. Everything else is convenience.

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Wallet (Breez Spark SDK)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# **Required.** API key for the Breez Spark SDK. Without it the SDK
# refuses to initialize and every wallet operation throws on boot.
# Read by `src/lib/wallet/client.ts:readEnvApiKey()` and passed to
# `connectWallet()`'s SDK config.
#
# Get one from Breez: https://docs.breez.technology
VITE_BREEZ_API_KEY=

# *Optional, currently unwired.* Override for the Breez Spark backend
# base URL — useful when routing through a staging mirror or local
# proxy. The SDK doesn't expose a base-URL knob in `defaultConfig`
# yet; this var is documented for forward-compat. No code reads it
# today.
# VITE_BREEZ_BASE_URL=https://api.breez.tech

# *Optional.* Pinned BIP-39 mnemonic for the **operator wallet only**.
# Scope:
#   - **Operator (header badge)**: read in `PhoenixHeader.tsx`. When
#     set, the operator wallet badge connects to this seed instead of
#     dev-only override for the operator envelope's `wallet.seed` (the
#     encrypted kind-30078 backup). Production app flows ignore this key.
#   - **`/dev/wallet` and `/dev/inference-pay` harnesses**: pre-fills
#     the mnemonic textbox so you can hit "Connect" without pasting
#     each refresh.
#   - **Personas (Dashboard badge)**: NOT subject to this override.
#     Each persona's badge always reads its own envelope seed so
#     donations land in the right wallet.
#
# Generate one by visiting `/dev/wallet`, clicking "Generate new",
# copying the seed, and pasting here. *Test funds only.*
# VITE_WALLET_SEED="abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon about"

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. PPQ (AI inference)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# PPQ credential pins are dev-only. Production operator flows ignore
# `VITE_PPQ_API_KEY` / `VITE_PPQ_CREDIT_ID` and use the operator envelope.
# Resolution chain:
#   1. dev-only env: VITE_PPQ_API_KEY (+ VITE_PPQ_CREDIT_ID)
#   2. operator envelope's `ppq` field
#   3. lazy-create on first AI request

# *Optional, dev-only.* Pinned PPQ API key. When set outside production,
# PPQ hooks skip the lazy-create-account flow and use this account directly.
# Useful for dev so a fresh browser doesn't burn a brand-new PPQ account
# each session — point it at an account you've already funded and reuse.
#
# Get one by:
#   - signing up at ppq.ai, or
#   - letting the app auto-create one once and copying the value out
#     of the encrypted operator envelope after auto-create
# VITE_PPQ_API_KEY=

# *Optional, recommended alongside `VITE_PPQ_API_KEY`.* Pinned PPQ
# `credit_id`. Required for balance lookup (the wallet panel's
# "credits" row) and for NWC auto-topup. Without it those features
# fail gracefully — chat completions and image generation still work.
# Pair with `VITE_PPQ_API_KEY` for a fully-wired dev account.
# VITE_PPQ_CREDIT_ID=

# *Optional.* PPQ API base URL. Defaults to `https://api.ppq.ai` if
# unset. Override only when proxying through a local dev server or
# hitting a staging environment. Read by `src/lib/ppq/client.ts`.
# VITE_PPQ_BASE_URL=https://api.ppq.ai

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. App / dev
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# *Optional, dev-only.* Pinned operator nsec for development. When set
# to a valid `nsec1…` AND no user is currently logged in, the
# `DevAutoLogin` component (`src/components/DevAutoLogin.tsx`) calls
# `useLoginActions().nsec(...)` once on boot. Falls back to the manual
# AuthDialog flow if unset, set to the literal placeholder
# `nsec1...`, or fails to decode.
#
# Dev-only — never set this in a production build. `VITE_*` vars are
# baked into the client bundle, so a pinned operator nsec would ship
# to every visitor.
#
# Scope: operator only. Persona nsecs are generated at creation time
# and stored in encrypted persona envelopes, never overridden.
# VITE_APP_USER_NSEC=nsec1...

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. Test scripts (Node-only, no VITE_ prefix)
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are read by interactive `tsx test/manual/<dir>/<script>.ts` runners
# in `test/manual/ai-services/` and `test/manual/wallet/`. They never reach the
# browser bundle. Documented here so the values aren't a surprise —
# leave most unset; the scripts have sensible defaults or interactive
# prompts.
#
# `test/manual/wallet/*.ts`:
#   These reuse `VITE_BREEZ_API_KEY` from the same `.env` (the wallet
#   client's `readEnv()` falls through to `process.env` in Node).
#
# `test/manual/ai-services/test-all-ppq-services-e2e.ts`:
#   PPQ_API_BASE          override for the PPQ HTTP base URL
#   PPQ_INVOICE_ID        skip create-topup-invoice; reuse this id
#   PPQ_INFERENCE_MODEL   override the chat-completion model (default: claude-sonnet-4.5)
#   PPQ_IMAGE_MODEL       override the image-gen model
#   PPQ_VIDEO_MODEL       override the video model (default: veo3-fast)
#
# `test/manual/ai-services/test-i2v-quick.ts` (image-to-video smoke):
#   PPQ_API_KEY           bearer key (NOTE: no VITE_ prefix here)
#   PPQ_IMAGE_URL         source image for the i2v test
#   PPQ_VIDEO_MODEL       defaults to `veo3.1-fast-i2v`
#   PPQ_PROMPT            video prompt
#   PPQ_ASPECT            "9:16" | "16:9" | "1:1" (default 9:16)
#   PPQ_DURATION          seconds (default 5)
#   PPQ_QUALITY           e.g. "720p"
